      "severity": "critical",
      "entry": 0,
      "title": "SHA-1 signature",
      "explanation": "The certificate or certificate signing request is signed with SHA-1, which is no longer collision resistant. Current software rejects SHA-1 certificate signatures, and a CA should refuse a SHA-1-signed request. On a self-signed CA certificate the signature is not checked when that certificate is used as a trust anchor, so there it is informational.",
      "evidence": [
        {
